## Update — gap-closing second pass (12 Jul 2026)

The first review fixed the first instance of each problem; this pass made it exhaustive. Per page: every residual flagged claim now has its own paste-ready quote + replacement (insurance wording repeated in FAQs, leftover safety/effectiveness phrasing, secondary GLP-1 mentions); all BMI/eligibility lines use the MBS-accurate framing (BMI 40+, or BMI 35–39.9 with a major comorbidity, always assessment-based); cut-lists are now full quoted passages with exact replacements; the missing Google-demand FAQ answers (cost in Perth, 30/30 rule, who is not eligible, Medicare, 10-year outcomes) are written AHPRA-safe; internal links point at real brief slugs; scaffolding artifacts are all flagged; and each page's brief has been corrected so the flagged wording doesn't recur. Per-page must/should-fix counts have grown accordingly — see each file.

Two review passes (Codex sol xhigh + independent second opinion) were run over the rework; all blocking findings applied. Quantified outcome stats (e.g. 60–70% / 70–80% excess-weight loss) are retained only as verify-gated notes, never as paste-ready copy.

Still OPEN (blocking final publication, not this review): hospital identity (briefs say SJOG Murdoch/Subiaco; drafts say Mount/The Park/Waikiki) and the GLP-1/medical-weight-management public-advertising policy (TGA/legal) — interim rule is class/ingredient names only, no brands.
