docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:189:Source line references below refer to `docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/extracted/bariatric-surgery-perth.md`.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:195:> Most bariatric surgeries in Australia are performed as laparoscopic keyhole surgeries, meaning less pain post-operatively, smaller scars, and generally, a faster recovery than open surgery. No procedure is a ‘one-size-fits-all’; your surgeon will spend time understanding your weight loss goals and recommend a procedure based on those, any accompanying health conditions, and your lifestyle.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:203:> Gastric bypass (Roux-en-Y): restricts food intake and changes how nutrients are absorbed. Typically results in greater weight loss than a sleeve, often ~70–80% of excess weight, though individual results will vary. Frequently preferred for type 2 diabetes due to its effect on blood sugar. Requires lifelong vitamin and mineral monitoring and supplementation.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:243:> A sleeve gastrectomy reduces the size of the stomach, leaving digestion otherwise unchanged. A gastric bypass does the same but also reroutes the small intestine, meaning the body absorbs fewer kilojoules from food. The bypass tends to produce slightly greater weight loss and stronger outcomes for type 2 diabetes and reflux, but is a more complex procedure with greater long-term nutritional demands. Your surgeon will help determine which is the better procedure for your situation.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:251:> Medicare rebates apply to most bariatric procedures when eligibility criteria are met, and private health insurance with a gold-tier or equivalent policy covers the hospital and theatre component. The combination of both typically means a significant portion of the total cost is covered. Out-of-pocket costs vary depending on your level of cover, excess, and anaesthetist fees. Our team provides a clear, itemised cost breakdown before any commitment is made, so you know exactly where you stand.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:255:Why it matters: This is a second coverage claim after the cost paragraph; it must not promise that a gold-tier policy covers a component or that a significant portion will be covered.
