docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:208:> **Replace the full cost section with one concise estimate/funding paragraph. Source: extracted draft L219-L236.**
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:210:> Gastric bypass surgery cost in Australia varies depending on your level of private health insurance cover, your surgeon and anaesthetist fees, hospital and theatre charges, and any out-of-pocket gap that applies to your situation. [Medicare item numbers 31572 and 31581](https://www9.health.gov.au/mbs/search.cfm?q=gastric+bypass&Submit=&sopt=S) attract a rebate when eligibility criteria are met, and private health insurance (typically a gold-tier or equivalent policy) covers the hospital and theatre component. Your surgeon's fee for a primary laparoscopic gastric bypass is $6,000 for both insured and uninsured patients, rising to $[X,XXX] for a complex case. For those without private health cover, or where out-of-pocket costs are a concern, superannuation may be accessible as a funding option in certain circumstances, including life-threatening conditions, certain psychiatric conditions, and the management of chronic pain. Financing options such as Zip and TLC are also available for eligible patients. A full breakdown of costs, funding pathways, and pre-surgical clinical fees can be found here.
