content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:55:> While it can be life-changing, weight loss surgery is a tool, not a one-off fix.
content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:59:Why it matters: "Life-changing" risks creating an unreasonable expectation of benefit under health advertising rules, even when the surrounding sentence is otherwise balanced.
content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:63:> **7. Does Medicare cover gastric sleeve surgery?** Medicare item number 31575 attracts a rebate when eligibility criteria are met, offsetting part of the surgical fee. However, Medicare alone doesn't cover the full cost and hospital, theatre, and anaesthetist fees still apply. Private health insurance with a gold-tier (or equivalent) policy will cover the hospital component. A full fee breakdown is available to help you understand your out-of-pocket costs.
content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:65:> **7. Does Medicare cover gastric sleeve surgery?** Medicare item 31575 may attract a rebate when the MBS requirements are met, but Medicare does not cover every fee. Hospital, theatre, surgeon and anaesthetist costs, private-health benefits and out-of-pocket gaps depend on your circumstances and policy, so confirm current details with your surgeon’s office and insurer. A consultation can help you understand which costs and rebates apply to you.
content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:79:> Weight loss outcomes vary between individuals; no specific result or timeline can be guaranteed.
content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:87:> Keyhole approach; means less scarring, generally less post-operative pain, and a shorter hospital stay (and recovery time) than open surgery.
content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:91:> Gastric sleeve surgery is well-established and generally safe, but it is still a major surgery which carries with it some real risks, all of which your surgeon will discuss with you in detail.
content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:97:> Staple line leak is a serious potential complication that may require further treatment; reported rates vary by patient and clinical setting, so ask your surgeon how this risk is monitored and managed.
content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:107:> **4. How is a gastric sleeve different from a gastric bypass?** A gastric sleeve reduces stomach size but leaves the digestive pathway unchanged. A gastric bypass both reduces the stomach *and* reroutes the small intestine, which can cause some nutrient malabsorption. The bypass may produce slightly greater weight loss and tends to suit patients with significant reflux better.
content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:115:Why it matters: These phrases imply guaranteed benefit, minimise risk, or make comparative safety/effectiveness claims. The replacements keep the information useful while making outcomes and recovery individual and measured.
