content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:153:> A gastric sleeve permanently reduces stomach size, a gastric bypass reduces stomach size and reroutes part of the small intestine, and prescription weight-management medicines, including GLP-1 medicines, work differently again; there is no single best option for everyone, and your surgeon can explain how reflux, BMI, diabetes, medication history and surgical risk affect the choice.
content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:161:> BMI is only a starting point. For Medicare item 31575, MBS eligibility generally requires a BMI of 40 or above, or BMI 35–39.9 with at least one major obesity-related condition — always subject to individual clinical assessment. Your surgeon will assess broader clinical risk, nutritional needs and ability to commit to aftercare; some conditions may need management first, and some people may not be suitable for surgery.
