content-briefs/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:73:- Para 3: Explain that most procedures are performed laparoscopically (keyhole), using small incisions. Do not make comparative pain, recovery or safety claims; explain that the surgeon will discuss the technique, expected recovery, alternatives and individual risks. Make clear that procedure choice is never one-size-fits-all — the surgeon advises based on weight, health conditions, eating patterns, and the patient's goals.
