    42	| 2 | perthbariatricsurgery.com.au | Perth Bariatric Surgery — Dr Andrew Kiyingi |
    43	| 3 | advancesurgical.com.au | Weight Loss Surgery Perth — Advance Surgical (Jon Armstrong) |
    44	| 4 | aurorabariatrics.com.au | Aurora Bariatrics — Dr Ruth Blackham |
    45	| 5 | obesitysurgerywa.com.au | Weight Loss Surgery Perth — Obesity Surgery WA (OSWA, DR 11) |
    46	
    47	### Content Gap Opportunity
    48	Every top result is a surgeon homepage that funnels straight to surgery — none present medical management (GLP-1 medication, VLCD, dietitian support) as an equal pathway. That is OSWA's biggest differentiation opportunity and aligns exactly with the brief's mandate to frame obesity as a medical condition and not over-index on surgery. Second gap: the PAA boxes show high demand for cost, Medicare coverage, and BMI/eligibility answers, yet competitor homepages bury or omit these — directly addressing how medical management is assessed from BMI 27+, how Medicare rebates and MBS thresholds work, and how much treatment may cost / whether superannuation access can be explored in plain language (the brief already mandates an eligibility section, cost paragraph, and FAQs) will capture featured-snippet and PAA real estate competitors leave open. Third gap: low-DR competitors mean strong topical depth, empathetic non-judgemental framing, and a team-based (dedicated APD dietitian team, physicians + surgeons, 2 clinics) angle can outrank them without heavy backlinks. Note OSWA (obesitysurgerywa.com.au) currently sits at position 5 with DR 11, so this page is an existing-asset improvement play, not a cold start.
    49	
    50	### Recommended Word Count
    51	1,100-1,400 words (matches brief; SERP is dominated by short-to-mid commercial clinic homepages, so the brief's depth is enough to compete while the spectrum-of-care breadth differentiates).
    52	
    53	## Section guidance
    54	
    55	### Hero
    56	- Headline direction: Frame the page as covering more than just surgery — it is about finding the right starting point. The headline should signal expertise and approachability in the same breath.
    57	- Subheadline: 2–3 sentences. Acknowledge the emotional reality of years of trying (without framing the reader as a failure). Introduce OSWA as a team — surgeons, physicians, and dietitians — not just a surgical service. Make clear the team meets the reader where they are, including if they are not yet ready for surgery.
    58	
    59	### Stats bar (4 stats)
